1
00:00:01,602 --> 00:00:03,337
EPISODE 17

2
00:00:15,516 --> 00:00:17,784
Gosh, this is… Oh, dear…

3
00:00:18,485 --> 00:00:22,155
Why are you all acting like this?
It makes me uncomfortable, okay?

4
00:00:22,222 --> 00:00:23,824
We're just worried about you.

5
00:00:23,891 --> 00:00:26,660
I'm really fine,
so you don't have to worry.

6
00:00:26,727 --> 00:00:28,095
What did Min-ho say?

7
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:32,399
He said it was enough
just to see his dad's face.

8
00:00:32,466 --> 00:00:35,269
He said for him,
just having his mom is enough.

9
00:00:35,936 --> 00:00:38,672
That rascal Min-ho
is much more mature than I am.

10
00:00:38,739 --> 00:00:40,274
That's a relief.

11
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:42,743
I was worried it might shock him.

12
00:00:42,809 --> 00:00:44,545
I know what you mean.

13
00:00:45,245 --> 00:00:47,781
So please stop worrying about us now.

14
00:00:48,448 --> 00:00:50,284
We've both done well so far.

15
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:52,986
And the two of us
will do great from now on.

16
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,390
I agreed to help Mr. Park
deliver his eggs today.

17
00:00:56,456 --> 00:00:58,025
-I'm heading out.
-Okay.

18
00:00:58,091 --> 00:00:59,626
I'll go with you.

19
00:00:59,693 --> 00:01:02,095
Forget it. Just do your own work.

20
00:01:02,162 --> 00:01:05,332
Our cabbages are full-grown.
I have nothing to do. Let's go.

21
00:01:05,399 --> 00:01:08,068
I said forget it.
What would you even do there…

22
00:01:08,135 --> 00:01:11,138
Come on, let's go, let's go, let's go!

23
00:01:11,204 --> 00:01:13,040
Wait, what'll you do there…

24
00:01:13,106 --> 00:01:14,741
We'll be back!

25
00:01:15,475 --> 00:01:16,677
ANIMAL WELFARE EGGS

26
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:18,679
By the way, what is this?

27
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:20,647
This?

28
00:01:20,714 --> 00:01:22,849
It's animal welfare certification.

29
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:24,451
Even farm animals, well,

30
00:01:24,518 --> 00:01:26,820
are given a happy life, basically.

31
00:01:26,887 --> 00:01:28,255
And this is the mark.

32
00:01:28,322 --> 00:01:31,625
So it means they're better eggs,
or something like that?

33
00:01:31,692 --> 00:01:32,826
Something like that.

34
00:01:32,893 --> 00:01:36,763
Then what this chicken symbolizes…
What kind of meaning does it…

35
00:01:36,830 --> 00:01:39,533
Come on, give it a rest now.

36
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:42,703
Stop putting on a whole show
just to cheer me up.

37
00:01:45,005 --> 00:01:46,273
Was it that obvious?

38
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:48,375
Your problem is you're so clumsy.

39
00:01:48,442 --> 00:01:50,377
You just can't do anything right.

40
00:01:51,078 --> 00:01:54,014
But are you really okay
with Min-ho's dad and all?

41
00:01:54,982 --> 00:01:58,151
I'd be lying
if I said I was really okay.

42
00:01:58,885 --> 00:02:02,089
But that's not his fault.

43
00:02:03,090 --> 00:02:06,560
He should get married, have kids too,

44
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:09,329
and live his own life.

45
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:14,401
I've never lived my life
expecting anything from him,

46
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:17,170
or wished he'd pop up like magic

47
00:02:17,237 --> 00:02:20,040
one day and take responsibility
for me and Min-ho.

48
00:02:21,375 --> 00:02:24,044
I just hope he's happy.

49
00:02:24,711 --> 00:02:27,080
And I hope Min-ho and I are happy too.

50
00:02:27,748 --> 00:02:30,784
You really are
the coolest single mom in the world.

51
00:02:33,487 --> 00:02:35,722
Thank you so much for yesterday.

52
00:02:36,757 --> 00:02:39,059
This shoulder is always free for you.

53
00:02:39,126 --> 00:02:41,428
Lean on it anytime.
You're always welcome.

54
00:02:42,429 --> 00:02:44,398
All right, thanks.

55
00:02:44,464 --> 00:02:46,199
Let's hurry, we're late.

56
00:02:48,335 --> 00:02:50,170
By the way, about Hyeok,

57
00:02:50,237 --> 00:02:52,205
doesn't he seem really into Yun-hui?

58
00:02:52,272 --> 00:02:54,007
He only looks out for Yun-hui.

59
00:02:54,074 --> 00:02:56,410
It's fishy how he follows her around.

60
00:02:57,377 --> 00:03:00,414
Come on, you punk.
What are you talking about?

61
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:02,449
She's older and even has a kid.

62
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:05,085
You're talking complete nonsense.

63
00:03:05,152 --> 00:03:06,987
Isn't that right, Min-gi?

64
00:03:07,921 --> 00:03:09,589
Maybe he does, maybe not.

65
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:11,825
It's none of my business.

66
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:21,334
There you go.

67
00:03:40,587 --> 00:03:41,688
Oh, right.

68
00:03:41,755 --> 00:03:43,890
What's with Yu-na? She's been gloomy.

69
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:46,693
Right, did you fight with Yu-na?

70
00:03:47,461 --> 00:03:49,096
It's nothing like that.

71
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:56,403
What's with this bastard again?

72
00:03:56,470 --> 00:03:59,072
They're all tragic heroes, all of them.

73
00:03:59,139 --> 00:04:00,774
You worry about others now?

74
00:04:00,841 --> 00:04:03,510
How's it going with you and Su-yeon?

75
00:04:04,444 --> 00:04:05,812
With me? Well,

76
00:04:05,879 --> 00:04:09,316
things couldn't be going any better.

77
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:12,853
Actually, a few days ago,
I even gave her a peck.

78
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:14,287
On the cheek.

79
00:04:15,655 --> 00:04:18,725
It's no exaggeration to call
Su-yeon my woman now.

80
00:04:18,792 --> 00:04:19,993
It's an exaggeration.

81
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:21,361
Such a fuss over a peck.

82
00:04:21,428 --> 00:04:24,564
A peck like that is just
a greeting in the United States.

83
00:04:24,631 --> 00:04:26,433
Just a hello when people meet.

84
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:28,602
You have to at least kiss

85
00:04:28,668 --> 00:04:31,037
to call yourselves a real couple.

86
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:34,174
A kiss? Come on, that's embarrassing.

87
00:04:34,241 --> 00:04:37,644
Wait, don't tell me you've never
even had your first kiss?

88
00:04:37,711 --> 00:04:39,679
You have, right?

89
00:04:39,746 --> 00:04:41,715
You punk, what do you take me for?

90
00:04:41,782 --> 00:04:44,117
I'm just kidding, there's no way.

91
00:04:44,184 --> 00:04:46,052
Seriously.

92
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,789
I never have.

93
00:04:51,024 --> 00:04:55,529
No first kiss even at your age?
What have you been doing?

94
00:04:56,363 --> 00:04:58,832
All right, you've already had a peck.

95
00:04:58,899 --> 00:05:02,502
Ride that momentum and go for a kiss.

96
00:05:03,336 --> 00:05:04,971
A kiss.

97
00:05:12,779 --> 00:05:15,182
Mom, please save me!

98
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:20,854
My ass.

99
00:05:20,921 --> 00:05:22,989
Is it because I'm in a different bed?

100
00:05:23,056 --> 00:05:25,358
Every time I sleep, it's a nightmare.

101
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:30,497
Anyway, I don't know
how long I have to stay here.

102
00:05:37,904 --> 00:05:39,573
Mi-yeong.

103
00:05:40,974 --> 00:05:43,743
How is it? Isn't it uncomfortable?

104
00:05:43,810 --> 00:05:48,215
Uncomfortable? It's comfier than home.
I slept like a baby.

105
00:05:48,281 --> 00:05:51,885
Don't do this, just go home.
Don't upset your mother.

106
00:05:53,587 --> 00:05:57,023
Let's just give up, honey.

107
00:05:57,858 --> 00:05:59,793
What are you talking about again?

108
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:02,462
Didn't I tell you to stop saying that?

109
00:06:02,529 --> 00:06:05,031
I'll convince my mom no matter what.

110
00:06:05,098 --> 00:06:07,300
So don't you worry at all, got it?

111
00:06:07,968 --> 00:06:09,369
Okay.

112
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:13,273
Here. I figured you missed breakfast,

113
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:14,808
so I made you some toast.

114
00:06:14,875 --> 00:06:16,142
Try some.

115
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:18,945
Wow, getting kicked out was worth it.

116
00:06:19,012 --> 00:06:21,915
I even get to try your cooking.

117
00:06:24,851 --> 00:06:27,187
Wow, this is delicious!

118
00:06:27,954 --> 00:06:30,724
I'm glad.
I'm off to work then. See you later.

119
00:06:30,790 --> 00:06:33,793
-All right, have a good day.
-Okay.

120
00:06:42,435 --> 00:06:45,839
Oh my, is this toast or gross?

121
00:06:46,506 --> 00:06:48,308
She really can't cook.

122
00:06:48,375 --> 00:06:52,078
Shouldn't I reconsider this marriage?

123
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:02,389
What's got you in such a good mood?

124
00:07:02,455 --> 00:07:04,124
What about me?

125
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:05,692
You said that Han-cheol guy

126
00:07:05,759 --> 00:07:09,162
or whoever made the outfit
you designed. Is that it?

127
00:07:09,696 --> 00:07:11,197
Huh?

128
00:07:11,264 --> 00:07:12,699
Yes.

129
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:14,634
That's suspicious.

130
00:07:14,701 --> 00:07:17,370
Wait, that Han-cheol guy or whoever,

131
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:19,172
did you fall head over heels?

132
00:07:19,239 --> 00:07:21,975
Fall for him? Stop talking nonsense.

133
00:07:23,176 --> 00:07:26,680
True, with a guy who looks like
a chewed-up dried radish,

134
00:07:26,746 --> 00:07:28,748
there's no way you'd fall for him.

135
00:07:28,815 --> 00:07:31,551
Anyway, he doesn't seem quite normal.

136
00:07:31,618 --> 00:07:32,886
How should I put it?

137
00:07:33,586 --> 00:07:36,790
Like he's a new kind of pervert?

138
00:07:36,856 --> 00:07:38,658
Why is Han-cheol a pervert?

139
00:07:38,725 --> 00:07:41,261
He's a kind and innocent person.

140
00:07:41,328 --> 00:07:43,964
You shouldn't judge people by looks.

141
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:46,366
Plus, what's wrong
with Han-cheol's looks?

142
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,468
He's plenty cute.

143
00:07:49,669 --> 00:07:52,005
I'm going alone today. Don't follow me.

144
00:07:52,072 --> 00:07:53,773
Oh my, oh my.

145
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,710
Look at her taking that guy's side.

146
00:07:56,776 --> 00:07:58,545
She fell for him, she really did.

147
00:07:59,212 --> 00:08:01,715
She's always negative about everything.

148
00:08:01,781 --> 00:08:05,518
Why say such mean things
to a kind, innocent person? Seriously.

149
00:08:07,954 --> 00:08:10,123
A kiss…

150
00:08:10,190 --> 00:08:13,893
So we have to kiss to be true lovers.

151
00:08:15,662 --> 00:08:19,699
Okay, I'll give Su-yeon my first kiss.

152
00:08:21,968 --> 00:08:25,905
Oh, but even if I ask,
Su-yeon probably won't do it…

153
00:08:28,575 --> 00:08:32,379
Big deal. If she won't,
I'll just play it cool and walk away.

154
00:08:33,313 --> 00:08:35,115
All right, let's go.

155
00:08:38,118 --> 00:08:39,519
Su-yeon!

156
00:08:39,586 --> 00:08:41,755
Han-cheol, what brings you here?

157
00:08:44,991 --> 00:08:47,660
I have a very small favor to ask…

158
00:08:47,727 --> 00:08:49,996
Yes? What is it?

159
00:08:50,063 --> 00:08:52,165
Well, I mean, um, it's…

160
00:08:54,234 --> 00:08:56,136
Ki…

161
00:08:57,604 --> 00:09:01,808
Kicture! No, a picture!
Could we paint together?

162
00:09:01,875 --> 00:09:03,610
Oh, paint a picture?

163
00:09:04,110 --> 00:09:05,445
Sure, go ahead.

164
00:09:12,652 --> 00:09:15,555
Where did they all go,
leaving me behind? How petty.

165
00:09:17,424 --> 00:09:18,458
What's this?

166
00:09:21,027 --> 00:09:22,462
What's this?

167
00:09:22,529 --> 00:09:26,166
My shoelace has never snapped before.

168
00:09:27,434 --> 00:09:29,402
Jeez, talk about bad luck.

169
00:09:34,474 --> 00:09:36,109
Oh?

170
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:38,845
How'd it go? Did you kiss?

171
00:09:38,912 --> 00:09:42,882
I have no idea what I'm supposed to do.

172
00:09:42,949 --> 00:09:46,519
I just went to see Su-yeon,
and all I did was paint a ton.

173
00:09:47,187 --> 00:09:49,255
Really? What was your plan?

174
00:09:49,322 --> 00:09:50,523
My plan?

175
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:54,027
I went up to say, "Su-yeon,
could you kiss me just once?"

176
00:09:54,094 --> 00:09:57,330
I tried to ask, but I just
couldn't get the words out.

177
00:09:57,397 --> 00:09:58,898
If the words had come out…

178
00:09:59,566 --> 00:10:01,367
Be glad the words didn't come out.

179
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:04,003
You would've gotten slapped for that.

180
00:10:04,070 --> 00:10:06,272
Who asks before kissing someone?

181
00:10:06,339 --> 00:10:07,841
Then how should I do it?

182
00:10:07,907 --> 00:10:09,476
Well, there's the normal way,

183
00:10:09,542 --> 00:10:11,878
or the fast track to do it in one shot.

184
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:13,813
-Which one?
-Fast track, definitely!

185
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:16,483
The fast track. Only one answer, then.

186
00:10:17,083 --> 00:10:20,320
Drinks. Alcohol makes people generous.

187
00:10:20,386 --> 00:10:22,322
It's perfect for setting the mood.

188
00:10:22,388 --> 00:10:25,325
-Wait for the right timing and--
-Drinks? Okay, okay!

189
00:10:25,391 --> 00:10:28,661
Wait, wait, wait!
Drinking alone isn't enough!

190
00:10:31,264 --> 00:10:32,465
Hwa-ran, where to?

191
00:10:32,532 --> 00:10:35,969
I'm on my way to town
to sell medicinal herbs.

192
00:10:36,035 --> 00:10:38,138
For your mother's hospital bills?

193
00:10:40,106 --> 00:10:42,609
Well, it's almost time for my bus,

194
00:10:42,675 --> 00:10:44,077
so I'll get going now.

195
00:10:44,944 --> 00:10:48,148
-Let's go together.
-I'm fine on my own.

196
00:10:48,214 --> 00:10:51,251
Don't get me wrong. I'm just curious…

197
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:53,186
about herbs, their local prices,

198
00:10:53,253 --> 00:10:56,789
and how distribution works.
That's the only reason I'm going.

199
00:10:57,624 --> 00:10:58,591
Let's go.

200
00:11:00,627 --> 00:11:02,262
Isn't that heavy for you?

201
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:05,031
-I'm fine.
-Let me carry it for you.

202
00:11:06,199 --> 00:11:08,067
Su-yeon.

203
00:11:10,937 --> 00:11:13,740
Han-cheol, why are you here again?

204
00:11:13,806 --> 00:11:14,974
Um…

205
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:18,011
Would you have a drink with me?

206
00:11:18,077 --> 00:11:20,980
Alcohol? In broad daylight?

207
00:11:21,614 --> 00:11:26,286
Actually, I have a serious problem.

208
00:11:27,053 --> 00:11:29,189
You were fine just a moment ago.

209
00:11:30,924 --> 00:11:33,226
I was just hiding it

210
00:11:33,293 --> 00:11:35,795
so you wouldn't worry.

211
00:11:35,862 --> 00:11:39,465
Then why are you telling me now?

212
00:11:41,768 --> 00:11:43,970
It's just that it simply…

213
00:11:45,438 --> 00:11:49,275
reached a state I can no longer bear.

214
00:11:50,143 --> 00:11:51,477
Oh…

215
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:55,448
But I'm not much of a drinker,
and I have so much painting to do.

216
00:11:59,752 --> 00:12:01,521
I see.

217
00:12:01,588 --> 00:12:03,690
Then it can't be helped, I guess.

218
00:12:03,756 --> 00:12:07,794
I'll just have to drink it all
by myself and pass out cold.

219
00:12:08,595 --> 00:12:12,265
Whether I go somewhere
and get into an accident or not,

220
00:12:12,332 --> 00:12:16,035
please don't worry about me.

221
00:12:30,783 --> 00:12:33,319
Fine, let's have a drink!

222
00:12:34,087 --> 00:12:36,022
Really?

223
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:37,924
Let's go together.

224
00:12:42,095 --> 00:12:45,765
Wait, you said we'd have a drink,
so why come all the way out here?

225
00:12:45,832 --> 00:12:48,268
I don't want others disturbing us.

226
00:12:48,334 --> 00:12:50,136
Just walk a little further.

227
00:12:50,203 --> 00:12:53,506
This spot is great. Have a seat here.

228
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:56,843
Please wait just a moment.

229
00:12:57,510 --> 00:12:59,312
Ta-da!

230
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:01,814
Ta-da!

231
00:13:04,484 --> 00:13:06,352
Here, please have a seat.

232
00:13:07,687 --> 00:13:09,255
What's the problem?

233
00:13:09,322 --> 00:13:12,125
First, please take a cup.

234
00:13:12,191 --> 00:13:13,626
It's hard to say sober

235
00:13:13,693 --> 00:13:15,395
because it's a serious problem.

236
00:13:15,962 --> 00:13:17,897
You like makgeolli, right?

237
00:13:22,902 --> 00:13:24,737
What on earth is it?

238
00:13:24,804 --> 00:13:26,806
First, drink this all down.

239
00:13:26,873 --> 00:13:28,808
Bottoms up, bottoms up first!

240
00:13:28,875 --> 00:13:31,377
Bottoms up, no brakes,
shake it over your head!

241
00:13:31,444 --> 00:13:32,979
Excuse me?

242
00:13:35,581 --> 00:13:39,786
Could you just do as I ask for today?

243
00:13:39,852 --> 00:13:41,487
All right, cheers!

244
00:13:48,895 --> 00:13:50,263
Whew!

245
00:13:53,066 --> 00:13:54,300
Are you happy now?

246
00:13:54,367 --> 00:13:55,635
Now, tell me.

247
00:13:55,702 --> 00:13:56,969
What's the problem?

248
00:13:57,770 --> 00:14:02,642
My problem is how to kiss you, Su-yeon.

249
00:14:03,609 --> 00:14:05,478
Let's talk after one more drink.

250
00:14:05,545 --> 00:14:08,414
I'm not getting tipsy. Have one more.

251
00:14:08,481 --> 00:14:11,651
I think I need to get a bit more tipsy
before I can talk.

252
00:14:11,718 --> 00:14:13,986
Drink up. Here, have some more. More.

253
00:14:18,758 --> 00:14:22,995
We dug up and sold so much,
and they only paid that measly amount?

254
00:14:23,062 --> 00:14:25,565
Still, they paid us plenty for this.

255
00:14:25,631 --> 00:14:28,501
Let's hurry up. It's time for the bus.

256
00:14:28,568 --> 00:14:31,604
Wait, wait. Let's stop somewhere first.

257
00:14:34,974 --> 00:14:37,710
Where are we going all of a sudden?

258
00:14:37,777 --> 00:14:40,313
Come on, you'll see when we get there.

259
00:14:41,114 --> 00:14:43,349
There it is.

260
00:14:46,386 --> 00:14:48,654
-Hello.
-Yes, welcome.

261
00:14:48,721 --> 00:14:50,790
-Let's see here.
-What can I get you?

262
00:14:50,857 --> 00:14:53,826
Oh? These look nice.

263
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:56,963
-Here, try them on.
-What? I don't need gloves.

264
00:14:57,029 --> 00:14:58,831
Just try them on like I said.

265
00:15:04,203 --> 00:15:06,472
Oh, they fit perfectly and look nice.

266
00:15:06,539 --> 00:15:07,974
-How much?
-10,000 won.

267
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:09,475
10,000 won.

268
00:15:09,542 --> 00:15:10,777
Yes, here you go.

269
00:15:10,843 --> 00:15:12,211
-Take care.
-Thank you.

270
00:15:12,278 --> 00:15:15,248
Be sure to wear these from now on
when you dig up herbs.

271
00:15:15,314 --> 00:15:18,050
You dig herbs barehanded,
so your hands are a mess.

272
00:15:18,818 --> 00:15:20,486
Ki-jun.

273
00:15:22,355 --> 00:15:23,689
Uh, don't get me wrong.

274
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:27,593
I just did it to, uh, help revitalize
the traditional market.

275
00:15:28,461 --> 00:15:31,230
It's not because I like you.

276
00:15:31,297 --> 00:15:34,233
Let's go. The bus is coming.
Grab your things.

277
00:15:47,013 --> 00:15:48,581
Don't get me wrong.

278
00:15:48,648 --> 00:15:51,451
I'm just testing how the gloves work.

279
00:15:51,517 --> 00:15:54,253
It's not because I like you.

280
00:15:55,655 --> 00:15:57,623
Let's go.

281
00:15:59,425 --> 00:16:01,294
Are the gloves any good?

282
00:16:02,862 --> 00:16:05,398
Don't let your hands get cold anymore.

283
00:16:17,176 --> 00:16:20,046
-Han-cheol!
-Yes?

284
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:23,449
Where am I?

285
00:16:23,516 --> 00:16:25,485
You looked like you were dozing off.

286
00:16:25,551 --> 00:16:27,186
Was I?

287
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:30,423
You said you couldn't drink,
but you drink so well.

288
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:31,657
Pardon?

289
00:16:32,258 --> 00:16:33,893
Um… I guess I do.

290
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:37,263
It must be going down smoothly today.

291
00:16:37,330 --> 00:16:40,900
But what on earth is troubling you?

292
00:16:41,601 --> 00:16:42,902
What's troubling me?

293
00:16:42,969 --> 00:16:44,937
Uh, what's troubling me is…

294
00:16:48,107 --> 00:16:50,610
My dilemma is that I wish to kiss you.

295
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:54,847
I want to kiss you. I want to kiss you.

296
00:16:55,648 --> 00:16:57,617
Oh, I want to kiss you.

297
00:17:01,487 --> 00:17:03,055
I want to kiss you!

298
00:17:03,823 --> 00:17:05,157
Excuse me?

299
00:17:05,224 --> 00:17:07,727
What did you just say?

300
00:17:07,793 --> 00:17:10,029
Pardon? What did I say?

301
00:17:10,096 --> 00:17:13,132
Um… did I say my thoughts out loud?

302
00:17:14,133 --> 00:17:16,569
Did you really ask me to get drinks

303
00:17:17,136 --> 00:17:18,871
just because of that?

304
00:17:18,938 --> 00:17:21,974
What? No, that's not it, um…

305
00:17:24,477 --> 00:17:26,045
Tell me.

306
00:17:26,546 --> 00:17:28,114
Honestly.

307
00:17:31,317 --> 00:17:32,552
Yes.

308
00:17:36,656 --> 00:17:39,892
Han-cheol, I thought you were
a kind and innocent person.

309
00:17:39,959 --> 00:17:41,794
I'm really disappointed in you.

310
00:17:43,296 --> 00:17:44,697
Su-yeon, I'm sorry.

311
00:17:44,764 --> 00:17:46,966
I must have lost my mind, Su-yeon.

312
00:17:47,033 --> 00:17:48,501
Su-yeon!

313
00:17:52,672 --> 00:17:53,906
Ta-da!

314
00:17:53,973 --> 00:17:56,108
Min-gi's special ramen is served!

315
00:17:56,175 --> 00:17:58,177
Wow, that looks delicious.

316
00:17:58,244 --> 00:18:00,947
Of course. I make killer ramen.

317
00:18:01,013 --> 00:18:04,483
The girls who tasted this
and wanted to marry me

318
00:18:04,550 --> 00:18:07,086
could line up across the Korea Strait.

319
00:18:07,153 --> 00:18:09,288
-Oh, please.
-Try it.

320
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:16,329
It's really delicious.

321
00:18:16,395 --> 00:18:18,931
It's so good because I made it, right?

322
00:18:18,998 --> 00:18:21,434
-So good.
-Have it with some kimchi too…

323
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:22,868
Did you expect perfume?

324
00:18:22,935 --> 00:18:25,438
Still, I liked being with you.

325
00:18:28,541 --> 00:18:30,843
Gosh, you two are having ramen.

326
00:18:30,910 --> 00:18:32,645
Mmm, that looks delicious.

327
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,148
Do you want some too?

328
00:18:36,215 --> 00:18:38,017
No, thanks, I'm good.

329
00:18:38,084 --> 00:18:40,319
Hyeok and I had a bowl of hangover soup

330
00:18:40,386 --> 00:18:43,389
on the way, so I'm stuffed. Dig in.

331
00:18:43,456 --> 00:18:45,391
Hyeok, good work today.

332
00:18:45,458 --> 00:18:46,459
Don't mention it.

333
00:18:46,525 --> 00:18:49,428
I'm using the computer
in your room like I said, okay?

334
00:18:49,495 --> 00:18:52,131
Hey! Hey, wait!

335
00:18:56,535 --> 00:18:58,170
Let's eat.

336
00:19:04,977 --> 00:19:07,580
Mom, I'm truly sorry.

337
00:19:07,647 --> 00:19:09,582
I know just how you feel.

338
00:19:09,649 --> 00:19:11,984
And I know accepting Mi-yeong is hard.

339
00:19:12,051 --> 00:19:15,788
But Mom, couldn't you give in
just once for your son?

340
00:19:16,422 --> 00:19:18,224
If you give in just this once,

341
00:19:18,290 --> 00:19:21,727
I'll give in to you
for the rest of my life, please?

342
00:19:23,062 --> 00:19:24,697
Mom.

343
00:19:24,764 --> 00:19:26,165
Mom.

344
00:19:26,232 --> 00:19:28,901
Let's talk face-to-face.

345
00:19:31,971 --> 00:19:33,739
You rotten bastard!

346
00:19:35,508 --> 00:19:38,010
Su-yeon, I'm truly sorry.

347
00:19:38,077 --> 00:19:40,379
I… must've lost my mind for a second.

348
00:19:40,446 --> 00:19:43,416
I said that's enough.
I have nothing to say to you.

349
00:19:44,316 --> 00:19:45,985
Su-yeon! Su-yeon!

350
00:19:46,052 --> 00:19:49,155
-Su-yeon!
-Stop following me!

351
00:19:49,221 --> 00:19:51,524
Su-yeon, come on! Please!

352
00:19:51,590 --> 00:19:53,459
Don't follow me in here!

353
00:19:53,526 --> 00:19:55,161
Su-yeon!

354
00:19:55,227 --> 00:19:56,829
What's the matter?

355
00:19:56,896 --> 00:19:58,731
No, it's nothing.

356
00:19:58,798 --> 00:20:00,499
Want some of these?

357
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:03,269
I don't want any. I don't want any.

358
00:20:03,335 --> 00:20:05,871
I'm already losing it!
Why do this too, Grandpa?

359
00:20:05,938 --> 00:20:09,275
If you don't want any, fine.
Why throw a fit, you punk?

360
00:20:09,942 --> 00:20:12,344
Should I go take a nap?

361
00:20:13,479 --> 00:20:15,781
Oh, my god! Whoa!

362
00:20:46,879 --> 00:20:48,447
Grandpa, are you okay?

363
00:20:48,514 --> 00:20:51,817
I'm fine, I'm fine.

364
00:20:52,485 --> 00:20:53,986
Are you okay?

365
00:21:04,563 --> 00:21:06,332
Are you crying?

366
00:21:07,733 --> 00:21:10,269
Why? Are you badly hurt?

367
00:21:10,336 --> 00:21:11,504
Huh?

368
00:21:15,474 --> 00:21:18,444
Why did an almond
come out of your mouth?

369
00:21:18,511 --> 00:21:19,712
Huh?

370
00:21:21,080 --> 00:21:23,082
Put it in here.

371
00:21:29,655 --> 00:21:31,824
Hey, man, what's wrong with you?

372
00:21:36,695 --> 00:21:40,232
Grandpa, I hate you! I hate you!

373
00:21:42,968 --> 00:21:45,404
My first kiss!

374
00:21:47,039 --> 00:21:50,009
Mr. Han, what are you doingsies?

375
00:21:50,676 --> 00:21:55,214
Thinking of you, Ms. Kim? Blush, blush.

376
00:21:55,848 --> 00:21:59,685
Stop it, Mr. Han. You're such a tease.

377
00:22:00,286 --> 00:22:02,621
You didn't forget our date, did you?

378
00:22:02,688 --> 00:22:06,592
Of course not! I didn't forgetsies.

379
00:22:09,662 --> 00:22:12,064
-Mom, what are you doing?
-I did nothingsies!

380
00:22:12,131 --> 00:22:14,066
"Did nothingsies, sies"?

381
00:22:14,733 --> 00:22:17,803
Mom, what's wrong?
Is your tongue twisted?

382
00:22:18,370 --> 00:22:21,407
Who did you keep texting like that?

383
00:22:21,473 --> 00:22:23,075
Did you get a boyfriend?

384
00:22:23,142 --> 00:22:25,177
It's not a boyfriend or anything.

385
00:22:25,244 --> 00:22:27,947
He's just a friend, a friend.

386
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:30,049
Since when do you have friends?

387
00:22:30,115 --> 00:22:33,419
You've been an outcast for 30 years
because of your big mouth.

388
00:22:33,485 --> 00:22:36,789
-I do have some! A few.
-You do?

389
00:22:36,856 --> 00:22:41,560
Your daughter ran away from home,
yet you're living the good life.

390
00:22:41,627 --> 00:22:43,529
It's not like that.

391
00:22:43,596 --> 00:22:46,265
But will you just leave I-ji alone?

392
00:22:46,332 --> 00:22:48,601
She walked out. Did I kick her out?

393
00:22:48,667 --> 00:22:50,603
Just leave that brat alone.

394
00:22:50,669 --> 00:22:53,205
She needs to suffer more. Much more.

395
00:22:53,272 --> 00:22:54,907
Don't be like that.

396
00:22:54,974 --> 00:22:56,942
Seems she'll work hard this time.

397
00:22:57,009 --> 00:22:59,445
Why not set her up with a coffee shop?

398
00:22:59,511 --> 00:23:02,681
I said forget it.
Don't I know that brat?

399
00:23:02,748 --> 00:23:05,284
That brat will last a few months again,

400
00:23:05,351 --> 00:23:08,187
then whine, "It's so hard," and quit.

401
00:23:08,254 --> 00:23:10,189
You think I don't know?

402
00:23:10,256 --> 00:23:11,991
Is anyone home?

403
00:23:12,057 --> 00:23:13,726
Who could that be?

404
00:23:13,792 --> 00:23:15,461
Who's there?

405
00:23:22,334 --> 00:23:25,237
Aw, we're here already.

406
00:23:26,105 --> 00:23:27,740
We sure are.

407
00:23:32,011 --> 00:23:34,546
I have to work now, so head on back.

408
00:23:35,047 --> 00:23:36,148
Okay, go on in.

409
00:23:37,816 --> 00:23:39,218
Let go of my hand first.

410
00:23:39,285 --> 00:23:41,186
Oh, right.

411
00:23:43,923 --> 00:23:46,058
Thank you so much for the gloves.

412
00:23:46,125 --> 00:23:50,029
Don't mention it. I'll get going.

413
00:24:07,913 --> 00:24:09,515
ALIEN ID CARD: WHAN-SI MIYANG

414
00:24:11,951 --> 00:24:13,285
It's valid. All cleared.

415
00:24:13,352 --> 00:24:15,321
See? I told you, didn't I?

416
00:24:15,387 --> 00:24:17,489
We have no, uh, illegal residents.

417
00:24:17,556 --> 00:24:20,693
We still must check. Please cooperate.

418
00:24:20,759 --> 00:24:22,561
No other foreign workers here?

419
00:24:22,628 --> 00:24:25,331
Who else? No, no. This is everyone.

420
00:24:25,397 --> 00:24:28,834
Hey, hey! Calm down!
They're not bad folks.

421
00:24:31,070 --> 00:24:32,604
And who is she?

422
00:24:33,339 --> 00:24:35,774
Oh, she's my daughter's friend, Bul-ja.

423
00:24:35,841 --> 00:24:38,677
Right, Bul-ja. Bul-ja, you're here!

424
00:24:38,744 --> 00:24:43,015
Aren't you calling her "Bul-ja"
as short for "illegal resident"?

425
00:24:49,021 --> 00:24:52,791
I'm just joking. I love a good joke.

426
00:24:54,093 --> 00:24:56,562
So funny! I nearly died laughing.

427
00:24:56,628 --> 00:24:58,297
-You could be a comic.
-You bet.

428
00:24:58,364 --> 00:25:00,366
I-ji's home. Let's hurry in, Bul-ja.

429
00:25:00,432 --> 00:25:01,734
Sure, sure. Go on in.

430
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:04,403
Gosh, they work so hard, these folks.

431
00:25:07,573 --> 00:25:10,209
-What should I do?
-Hurry, go home and hide.

432
00:25:10,275 --> 00:25:12,878
Okay, I'll go on ahead, then.

433
00:25:12,945 --> 00:25:15,180
Hold on a moment.

434
00:25:17,249 --> 00:25:18,150
ENFORCEMENT

435
00:25:18,217 --> 00:25:21,053
Your accent is odd. Let's see your ID.

436
00:25:23,555 --> 00:25:25,290
You don't have an ID?

437
00:25:26,291 --> 00:25:28,293
You're an illegal resident, right?

438
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:29,828
Aren't you?

439
00:25:40,839 --> 00:25:42,508
Stop right there!

440
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:44,810
Hwa-ran?

441
00:25:44,877 --> 00:25:47,579
I said stop! Stop right there!

442
00:25:47,646 --> 00:25:50,382
-What's going on?
-It's immigration!

443
00:25:50,449 --> 00:25:52,484
If I get caught, I'll be deported.

444
00:25:52,551 --> 00:25:54,620
I'll handle this, so hurry and go.

445
00:25:54,686 --> 00:25:55,883
Hurry, go!

446
00:25:55,958 --> 00:25:57,856
I'll handle this, so hurry! Go, go!

447
00:25:57,923 --> 00:26:00,292
What's with this guy?

448
00:26:00,359 --> 00:26:02,494
Let go! Let go of me!

449
00:26:05,731 --> 00:26:07,066
What is this? Jeez!

450
00:26:07,132 --> 00:26:09,001
Hey, mister! Move! Hurry, hurry!

451
00:26:09,068 --> 00:26:11,603
Yes, okay. I'll move it, I'll move it.

452
00:26:11,670 --> 00:26:13,872
What are you doing? Move forward now!

453
00:26:13,939 --> 00:26:15,140
I think it broke down.

454
00:26:15,207 --> 00:26:18,544
Hey, you people! You'll regret this.

455
00:26:20,179 --> 00:26:22,081
That's obstruction of duty, got it?

456
00:26:24,716 --> 00:26:26,852
Sir, what do we do about Hwa-ran?

457
00:26:27,519 --> 00:26:30,155
I know. I hope she doesn't get caught.

458
00:26:30,222 --> 00:26:32,157
Darn it, seriously!

459
00:26:53,178 --> 00:26:54,613
Oh, Min-ho.

460
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:57,983
How does 47 minus 35 make 22? It's 12.

461
00:26:58,617 --> 00:27:00,219
Oh, right, right. My mistake.

462
00:27:00,285 --> 00:27:03,288
You always say it's a mistake.

463
00:27:03,355 --> 00:27:06,558
He's good at everything else,
but math is still a problem.

464
00:27:06,625 --> 00:27:08,894
You're right. Everything else is fine.

465
00:27:08,961 --> 00:27:10,896
But math is a bit tricky, Yun-hui.

466
00:27:10,963 --> 00:27:13,031
Then should I tutor him in math?

467
00:27:13,098 --> 00:27:14,766
I'm a med student. I know math.

468
00:27:14,833 --> 00:27:16,668
Hey, forget it. Just forget it.

469
00:27:16,735 --> 00:27:19,104
You saying that makes me deeply uneasy.

470
00:27:19,171 --> 00:27:20,973
Still, as if I'd fail kids' math…

471
00:27:21,039 --> 00:27:23,442
Trust me, I'll make him a math genius.

472
00:27:23,509 --> 00:27:26,078
Min-ho, you'll study math
with me tomorrow, okay?

473
00:27:26,145 --> 00:27:27,779
Okay!

474
00:27:30,382 --> 00:27:33,185
Oh my, it's already this late.

475
00:27:33,252 --> 00:27:35,420
Min-ho, it's bedtime. Go wash up.

476
00:27:35,487 --> 00:27:36,588
-Okay, Mom.
-Okay.

477
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:39,324
Up we go, up, up!

478
00:27:41,093 --> 00:27:44,830
Yun-hui, have you heard
from Min-ho's dad since then?

479
00:27:45,597 --> 00:27:47,199
No, I haven't.

480
00:27:47,266 --> 00:27:48,834
After you came back like that,

481
00:27:48,901 --> 00:27:51,136
how can he not even call once?

482
00:27:51,803 --> 00:27:53,605
He must have his reasons.

483
00:27:53,672 --> 00:27:56,441
Besides, I don't even expect that.

484
00:27:56,508 --> 00:27:58,844
Still, he's going too far.

485
00:27:58,911 --> 00:28:00,479
If he found out he has a kid,

486
00:28:00,546 --> 00:28:03,215
he should've at least called once.

487
00:28:03,282 --> 00:28:05,684
That rotten bastard.

488
00:28:08,620 --> 00:28:12,691
-Han-cheol, you're back? What's wrong?
-Hey, what's with you? Are you crying?

489
00:28:12,758 --> 00:28:16,695
Don't ask me anything!
Don't ask me anything, darn it!

490
00:28:18,964 --> 00:28:22,935
-Gosh, what's wrong with him?
-What's gotten into him?

491
00:28:24,169 --> 00:28:25,837
Oh, honestly.

492
00:28:27,239 --> 00:28:30,609
Hello? Yes, ma'am. Yes.

493
00:28:31,276 --> 00:28:34,246
What? Bul-ja? When?

494
00:28:34,913 --> 00:28:36,215
Why? What about Bul-ja?

495
00:28:36,281 --> 00:28:38,984
Immigration came,
and she says Bul-ja ran away.

496
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:41,019
What?

497
00:28:41,086 --> 00:28:43,922
Yes, I'll be right there. Yes, okay.

498
00:28:43,989 --> 00:28:44,957
Oh, honestly.

499
00:28:45,023 --> 00:28:48,527
I can't just stay here.
I'll run over to Man-gu's place.

500
00:28:55,133 --> 00:28:57,569
Oh dear, what do we do? What do we do?

501
00:28:57,636 --> 00:28:59,671
Our poor Bul-ja, what do we do?

502
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:01,840
Please, that's enough now.

503
00:29:01,907 --> 00:29:04,843
Just be thankful she wasn't caught.

504
00:29:05,978 --> 00:29:07,813
You should head back too.

505
00:29:07,879 --> 00:29:10,048
How long will you stay like that?

506
00:29:10,115 --> 00:29:12,017
I'll wait until Hwa-ran comes back.

507
00:29:12,084 --> 00:29:13,585
How can she come back here?

508
00:29:13,652 --> 00:29:15,854
Immigration is still staked out here.

509
00:29:15,921 --> 00:29:18,123
She can't ever come back here.

510
00:29:18,190 --> 00:29:19,524
You hear me?

511
00:29:19,591 --> 00:29:22,160
Just give up and go on inside.

512
00:29:24,930 --> 00:29:26,765
I told you to go!

513
00:29:26,832 --> 00:29:29,601
I didn't even get to say goodbye.

514
00:29:32,337 --> 00:29:35,474
She even dropped her gloves.
Her hands must be so cold…

515
00:30:56,755 --> 00:30:59,291
I LOVE YOU

516
00:31:14,406 --> 00:31:16,575
What is that? What are you doing?

517
00:31:19,478 --> 00:31:23,048
Go, go! Get out of here!

518
00:31:30,889 --> 00:31:32,157
What's this?

519
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:36,862
What is it now?

520
00:31:36,928 --> 00:31:40,832
I went to the mountain for herbs
and gathered some wild cliff honey.

521
00:31:43,902 --> 00:31:45,670
It is your birthday gift, Ki-jun.

522
00:31:51,109 --> 00:31:54,413
Are you all right? Let me see.

523
00:31:54,479 --> 00:31:56,948
It is Hwa-ran. Song Hwa-ran.

524
00:31:57,015 --> 00:31:59,651
My name is not Bul-ja.
It is Song Hwa-ran.

525
00:31:59,718 --> 00:32:02,854
Bul-ja, come on out.

526
00:32:13,165 --> 00:32:14,800
Just take one picture.

527
00:32:14,866 --> 00:32:17,302
Seeing a photo of you two
as friends here,

528
00:32:17,369 --> 00:32:20,639
how happy will Bul-ja's mom be
that she's doing well?

529
00:32:53,772 --> 00:32:56,308
What happened to Bul-ja?

530
00:32:56,975 --> 00:32:59,144
Luckily, I don't think she got caught.

531
00:32:59,211 --> 00:33:02,781
But there's no telling where she went.

532
00:33:04,049 --> 00:33:06,451
I doubt she'll come back to this town.

533
00:33:06,518 --> 00:33:08,286
How is Ki-jun doing?

534
00:33:08,353 --> 00:33:11,523
He's stubbornly insisting
on waiting there for Bul-ja.

535
00:33:11,590 --> 00:33:14,426
Poor Bul-ja, what will become of her?

536
00:33:14,493 --> 00:33:16,161
I know, really.

537
00:33:16,228 --> 00:33:20,866
She went through so much
to support her family. What a shame.

538
00:33:26,104 --> 00:33:27,539
-Hello.
-Hi there.

539
00:33:27,606 --> 00:33:28,974
Come on, we were waiting.

540
00:33:29,040 --> 00:33:30,842
What about Ki-jun?

541
00:33:31,877 --> 00:33:33,178
He says he won't eat.

542
00:33:33,245 --> 00:33:36,882
I'm worried about him.
He's barely eaten for days.

543
00:33:36,948 --> 00:33:39,518
It's obviously because of Bul-ja.

544
00:33:39,584 --> 00:33:42,787
Anyway, I wonder if Bul-ja is okay.

545
00:33:43,588 --> 00:33:45,590
Next up, ahead of kimchi season,

546
00:33:45,657 --> 00:33:48,660
cabbage prices plunged,
deepening farmers' worries.

547
00:33:48,727 --> 00:33:49,995
Kim Jun-su reports.

548
00:33:50,996 --> 00:33:54,866
Kimchi-season cabbage prices
fell below 1,000 won per head.

549
00:33:54,933 --> 00:33:56,668
-Supply is high…
-What is that?

550
00:33:56,735 --> 00:33:59,104
Even a price rebound seems unlikely.

551
00:33:59,170 --> 00:34:00,906
What is that?

552
00:34:00,972 --> 00:34:03,975
Unable to even cover harvest costs,

553
00:34:04,042 --> 00:34:06,978
farmers are even plowing under
the cabbage fields they grew.

554
00:34:07,712 --> 00:34:09,548
CABBAGE PRICES

555
00:34:13,985 --> 00:34:16,488
CABBAGE CRASH:
15,000 WON A HEAD, NOW 100 WON?

556
00:34:17,422 --> 00:34:20,125
So the farming area grew this year,

557
00:34:20,191 --> 00:34:23,395
and good weather boosted production.

558
00:34:23,461 --> 00:34:26,231
As a result, there's too much supply,

559
00:34:26,298 --> 00:34:28,066
so prices were bound to crash.

560
00:34:28,133 --> 00:34:31,469
This is impossible. Just impossible.

561
00:34:32,637 --> 00:34:35,106
Hey, how did this happen?

562
00:34:35,941 --> 00:34:38,209
You said prices rise in kimchi season!

563
00:34:38,276 --> 00:34:41,413
You said prices would go up, huh?

564
00:34:44,115 --> 00:34:45,283
Hey.

565
00:34:46,484 --> 00:34:49,654
Hey, say something, you bastard!

566
00:34:54,859 --> 00:34:57,429
What are you guys talking about?

567
00:34:59,264 --> 00:35:01,199
Hey, Ki-jun.

568
00:35:01,967 --> 00:35:05,303
They say cabbage prices crashed.
They crashed.

569
00:35:05,370 --> 00:35:07,906
What do you mean…

570
00:35:08,840 --> 00:35:12,377
No, this can't be happening.

571
00:35:13,845 --> 00:35:15,547
This can't be happening!

572
00:35:17,916 --> 00:35:19,317
Min-gi!

573
00:35:19,384 --> 00:35:21,419
Jeez, seriously.

574
00:35:35,400 --> 00:35:38,536
Hey, isn't there still a way?

575
00:35:38,603 --> 00:35:39,838
What way is there?

576
00:35:39,904 --> 00:35:43,108
They say even at retail,
it's not even 1,000 won a head.

577
00:35:43,174 --> 00:35:45,577
-Not even 1,000 won.
-I know, but still.

578
00:35:45,644 --> 00:35:49,347
If we sell all 100,000 heads,
wouldn't that make a nice lump sum?

579
00:35:49,414 --> 00:35:50,882
How on earth do we sell it?

580
00:35:50,949 --> 00:35:54,019
We can just load it ourselves
and go sell it in Seoul.

581
00:35:56,421 --> 00:35:58,790
Sell 100,000 cabbages by ourselves?

582
00:35:58,857 --> 00:36:00,625
That'd take over a year. A year!

583
00:36:00,692 --> 00:36:02,627
All this cabbage will rot, punk!

584
00:36:02,694 --> 00:36:07,132
And what about harvest labor costs?
What about gas for the truck?

585
00:36:07,198 --> 00:36:11,202
After deducting all those expenses,
there's nothing left, nothing at all!

586
00:36:11,269 --> 00:36:12,904
Darn it, seriously.

587
00:36:13,705 --> 00:36:15,740
Hey, you take responsibility.

588
00:36:17,475 --> 00:36:19,444
You take responsibility, you bastard!

589
00:36:19,511 --> 00:36:21,112
Hey, Han-cheol! Stop it.

590
00:36:21,813 --> 00:36:23,381
Stop? Why should I stop?

591
00:36:23,448 --> 00:36:25,917
Do you know how I felt
following you all here?

592
00:36:25,984 --> 00:36:28,219
Do you know how I felt
coming down here?

593
00:36:28,286 --> 00:36:30,055
I know, I know, so just stop.

594
00:36:30,121 --> 00:36:32,257
You think you know?

595
00:36:32,323 --> 00:36:33,992
You all know how I feel?

596
00:36:34,826 --> 00:36:37,295
No, you guys don't know.

597
00:36:37,362 --> 00:36:39,764
You'll never know how I feel, darn it!

598
00:36:39,831 --> 00:36:41,232
Screw this!

599
00:36:43,468 --> 00:36:45,136
Han-cheol!

600
00:36:48,006 --> 00:36:49,908
I'm sorry.

601
00:36:52,110 --> 00:36:53,712
I'm really sorry.

602
00:36:53,778 --> 00:36:56,681
Was it last year? Happened to me too.

603
00:36:56,748 --> 00:37:00,652
I worked tirelessly all year
without a break to grow my crops.

604
00:37:01,319 --> 00:37:04,155
But onion prices crashed,

605
00:37:04,222 --> 00:37:05,957
so I had to plow it all under.

606
00:37:06,024 --> 00:37:08,359
That's just how farming is.

607
00:37:08,426 --> 00:37:11,896
Too little is a problem,
and too much is a problem.

608
00:37:11,963 --> 00:37:14,432
Good weather is a problem.
Bad weather is too.

609
00:37:14,499 --> 00:37:17,168
Still, won't prices go up if we wait?

610
00:37:17,235 --> 00:37:18,803
Well, there's no telling.

611
00:37:18,870 --> 00:37:22,674
But if you miss the shipping window,
it's a complete bust.

612
00:37:22,741 --> 00:37:25,410
Their market value is zero. Zero.

613
00:37:25,477 --> 00:37:27,712
It's heartbreaking,
but what can you do?

614
00:37:28,913 --> 00:37:30,148
Just give up.

615
00:37:32,117 --> 00:37:33,852
What do you mean, give up?

616
00:37:34,652 --> 00:37:36,221
After all our work growing it?

617
00:37:36,287 --> 00:37:38,456
Do you know what we did to grow these?

618
00:37:43,161 --> 00:37:45,196
Damn it…

619
00:37:49,167 --> 00:37:52,971
How come that Han-cheol guy
or whatever hasn't shown up today?

620
00:37:53,037 --> 00:37:54,873
Don't even bring that guy up.

621
00:37:54,939 --> 00:37:58,176
You defended him so much yesterday.

622
00:37:58,243 --> 00:37:59,611
What's with you today?

623
00:37:59,677 --> 00:38:02,781
Anyway, I'm never going to care
about that guy again.

624
00:38:10,221 --> 00:38:13,158
What's wrong? Why are they so down?

625
00:38:20,532 --> 00:38:23,935
Sir, um… is something wrong?

626
00:38:24,536 --> 00:38:27,105
Cabbage prices completely crashed.

627
00:38:27,172 --> 00:38:30,608
All the farming those boys did
ended up being for nothing.

628
00:38:31,109 --> 00:38:33,511
-Really?
-That's right.

629
00:38:33,578 --> 00:38:36,681
Those young fellows wanted to make
an album or whatever,

630
00:38:36,748 --> 00:38:38,850
and worked themselves half to death.

631
00:38:38,917 --> 00:38:40,218
Oh, gosh.

632
00:38:40,285 --> 00:38:44,322
But why isn't that Han-cheol guy
or whatever his name is around?

633
00:38:44,389 --> 00:38:46,791
Han-cheol was so terribly upset

634
00:38:46,858 --> 00:38:49,227
that he ran off screaming like crazy.

635
00:38:50,128 --> 00:38:53,264
I'm afraid he'll do something
reckless out of anger.

636
00:38:53,331 --> 00:38:55,233
Oh, gosh.

637
00:38:58,636 --> 00:39:00,972
Hey, I need to go somewhere quickly.

638
00:39:01,039 --> 00:39:02,407
Huh?

639
00:39:17,155 --> 00:39:19,123
Han-cheol!

640
00:39:20,558 --> 00:39:23,862
I heard what happened. Are you okay?

641
00:39:23,928 --> 00:39:25,096
No.

642
00:39:26,097 --> 00:39:27,498
I'm not okay.

643
00:39:31,002 --> 00:39:33,037
Su-yeon, what do I do now?

644
00:39:37,775 --> 00:39:41,646
What am I supposed to do now, Su-yeon?

645
00:40:10,141 --> 00:40:12,010
Oh, Min-gi!

646
00:40:15,346 --> 00:40:17,348
Min-gi, are you okay?

647
00:40:18,483 --> 00:40:19,784
We're okay.

648
00:40:19,851 --> 00:40:21,185
Min-gi, um…

649
00:40:21,252 --> 00:40:24,989
Yu-na, let's talk later. Later.

650
00:41:45,203 --> 00:41:47,739
Hey, don't look at me like that.

651
00:41:47,805 --> 00:41:50,141
Because looking at your mug annoys me!

652
00:41:50,742 --> 00:41:53,077
All right, since it's come to this,

653
00:41:53,144 --> 00:41:55,947
let's find out where rock bottom is.

654
00:41:56,014 --> 00:41:58,349
But when will we ever harvest all this?

655
00:41:59,250 --> 00:42:00,918
You'll give it your all, right?

656
00:42:00,985 --> 00:42:03,354
-I'm in!
-Okay.

657
00:42:18,169 --> 00:42:19,771
Guys!

658
00:42:20,438 --> 00:42:21,839
Yun-hui!

659
00:42:21,906 --> 00:42:24,308
What brings you all out here?

660
00:42:24,375 --> 00:42:27,078
I just had nothing better to do.

661
00:42:27,145 --> 00:42:29,947
All I'd do is drink makgeolli, right?

662
00:42:31,082 --> 00:42:33,251
I got kicked out too,
with nothing to do.

663
00:42:33,317 --> 00:42:35,653
What are you standing there staring at?

664
00:42:35,720 --> 00:42:38,189
We have a mountain of work.
Hurry up and cut!

665
00:42:38,890 --> 00:42:41,325
-I'm in!
-All right, let's do this!

666
00:42:56,541 --> 00:42:59,977
We'll try to find a way too,
so hang in there, guys.

667
00:43:00,044 --> 00:43:02,547
-Thank you so much.
-Don't get your hopes up.

668
00:43:02,613 --> 00:43:04,782
High hopes lead to big disappointment.

669
00:43:04,849 --> 00:43:06,384
Let's get going.

670
00:43:21,933 --> 00:43:25,002
You guys head back too.
I'll stay a bit longer.

671
00:43:27,705 --> 00:43:28,940
All right.

672
00:43:30,074 --> 00:43:32,844
Don't stay out here alone too long.

673
00:43:33,511 --> 00:43:34,812
We'll go on ahead.

674
00:44:04,509 --> 00:44:06,043
You're back?

675
00:44:07,078 --> 00:44:10,348
-Where is Min-gi?
-Don't know. He said he'd come later.

676
00:44:12,850 --> 00:44:15,153
By the way, where's Yun-hui?

677
00:44:15,219 --> 00:44:16,320
Huh?

678
00:44:17,021 --> 00:44:18,589
She isn't back yet.

679
00:44:19,690 --> 00:44:22,360
I'm going to go check on Min-gi.

680
00:44:26,564 --> 00:44:29,667
Where'd she go? She left ahead of us.

681
00:44:54,258 --> 00:44:56,928
Stop crying, you punk. Stop it, okay?

682
00:44:56,994 --> 00:44:58,563
Oh, goodness.

683
00:44:58,629 --> 00:45:01,432
You bragged like you could
take on the whole world.

684
00:45:01,499 --> 00:45:04,335
Did the great Lee Min-gi
chicken out over just this?

685
00:45:14,145 --> 00:45:15,146
Hang in there.

686
00:45:15,213 --> 00:45:17,548
It's not over yet.

687
00:45:17,615 --> 00:45:19,750
I'll find a way somehow.

688
00:45:19,817 --> 00:45:21,652
So don't worry, okay?

689
00:45:23,888 --> 00:45:24,989
Darn it.

690
00:45:25,056 --> 00:45:27,258
Gosh, stop crying already.

691
00:45:27,325 --> 00:45:31,028
You acted so tough,
but you're a total softie, aren't you?

692
00:45:32,897 --> 00:45:36,300
Oh, stop it. Gosh, you look awful.

693
00:45:56,254 --> 00:45:57,888
This is getting complicated.

694
00:45:59,357 --> 00:46:01,993
-What do you mean?
-Why ask when you know?

695
00:46:07,598 --> 00:46:10,901
Gosh, how can you sniffle so grossly?

696
00:46:10,968 --> 00:46:13,671
Sniffling like that. Gosh, your nose…

697
00:46:14,939 --> 00:46:18,009
-Yu-na.
-Can we talk?

698
00:46:21,979 --> 00:46:24,215
I'll head inside first, then.

699
00:46:31,722 --> 00:46:34,625
-About what?
-Am I really misunderstanding this?

700
00:46:34,692 --> 00:46:36,260
What are you talking about?

701
00:46:36,327 --> 00:46:39,163
-Is this about Yun-hui again?
-I saw everything.

702
00:46:39,797 --> 00:46:41,732
You two in the cabbage field.

703
00:46:43,434 --> 00:46:44,802
Well…

704
00:46:45,369 --> 00:46:47,705
I was upset and having a hard time.

705
00:46:47,772 --> 00:46:51,175
-Yun-hui was just comforting me--
-Why Yun-hui and not me?

706
00:46:51,242 --> 00:46:53,544
You always told me you were fine.

707
00:46:53,611 --> 00:46:56,480
Why show Yun-hui your true feelings?

708
00:46:56,547 --> 00:46:57,682
-Huh--
-When you hurt

709
00:46:57,748 --> 00:47:01,285
why is Yun-hui the one you lean on
for comfort instead of me?

710
00:47:01,919 --> 00:47:03,321
That's…

711
00:47:03,387 --> 00:47:06,223
I don't want to misunderstand either.

712
00:47:06,290 --> 00:47:08,626
I keep feeling
it's not a misunderstanding.

713
00:47:08,693 --> 00:47:10,227
What do you mean it's not?

714
00:47:10,294 --> 00:47:12,430
Do you really not know what I mean?

715
00:47:14,999 --> 00:47:17,301
Then think it over carefully.

716
00:47:19,704 --> 00:47:21,572
Yu-na!

717
00:47:26,077 --> 00:47:29,246
Can you guys really do this well?

718
00:47:29,313 --> 00:47:31,682
We have to try somehow.

719
00:47:31,749 --> 00:47:34,185
Um, by the way, where's Yu-na?

720
00:47:34,251 --> 00:47:37,088
I don't know.
She's holed up in her room all day.

721
00:47:37,154 --> 00:47:38,989
Did you two have a fight?

722
00:47:39,056 --> 00:47:41,058
No, it's nothing like that.

723
00:47:43,194 --> 00:47:45,796
I'm worried, though.
You've never sold anything.

724
00:47:45,863 --> 00:47:48,432
-Should I just come along--
-No, we're fine.

725
00:47:48,499 --> 00:47:49,934
We'll go by ourselves.

726
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:52,169
Let's go. We'll be back.

727
00:47:52,236 --> 00:47:53,537
We'll see you later.

728
00:47:53,604 --> 00:47:55,373
Ouch…

729
00:47:59,610 --> 00:48:03,214
Take care. Buckle up in the back too.

730
00:48:03,280 --> 00:48:04,648
Be careful.

731
00:48:07,151 --> 00:48:09,520
Have a safe trip!

732
00:48:27,238 --> 00:48:28,639
PRETTY MIN-A

733
00:48:28,706 --> 00:48:32,443
Please call me right away.
It's really important.

734
00:48:36,313 --> 00:48:38,883
Hello? What's going on?

735
00:48:38,949 --> 00:48:43,287
Um, well, you see…

736
00:48:44,588 --> 00:48:46,223
It's me.

737
00:48:47,458 --> 00:48:48,726
CEO?

738
00:48:48,793 --> 00:48:52,329
Where are you? What are you doing?
Get back up here right now.

739
00:48:53,864 --> 00:48:57,168
And if I come back up?
You have no use for me anymore.

740
00:48:57,835 --> 00:48:59,170
Let's go overseas.

741
00:48:59,236 --> 00:49:01,472
Let's move up the plans we put off.

742
00:49:02,440 --> 00:49:04,675
Go overseas?

743
00:49:04,742 --> 00:49:06,811
Ma'am, buy some cabbages. Take a look!

744
00:49:06,877 --> 00:49:09,447
-They're very fresh.
-Buy some cabbages, ma'am.

745
00:49:09,513 --> 00:49:12,016
Ready to make kimchi, ma'am?
Buy some cabbages.

746
00:49:12,082 --> 00:49:14,785
-Buy some cabbages.
-Take a look at our cabbages.

747
00:49:14,852 --> 00:49:17,621
Hello, ma'am.
Come take a look at our cabbages.

748
00:49:17,688 --> 00:49:19,990
Miss, pretty lady, buy some cabbages!

749
00:49:23,327 --> 00:49:24,895
Hey.

750
00:49:25,863 --> 00:49:28,899
Here, we should at least eat this.

751
00:49:29,567 --> 00:49:33,471
We've been selling all day
and haven't even sold half.

752
00:49:33,537 --> 00:49:34,705
Maybe drop the price?

753
00:49:34,772 --> 00:49:37,508
Hey, then we won't even cover gas.

754
00:49:37,575 --> 00:49:40,945
Still, let's do all we can. Let's go!

755
00:49:41,011 --> 00:49:43,080
-Let's go.

756
00:49:48,252 --> 00:49:49,553
Ki-jun.

757
00:49:50,054 --> 00:49:52,490
-Let's stop.
-Stop? What do you mean, dude?

758
00:49:52,556 --> 00:49:56,393
I know it's hopeless to keep going,
and you guys all know it too.

759
00:49:56,460 --> 00:49:59,330
-Dude, still…
-Still!

760
00:50:00,564 --> 00:50:02,533
We should have hope?

761
00:50:02,600 --> 00:50:05,102
What hope? What hope do we even have?

762
00:50:05,169 --> 00:50:07,137
Tell me.

763
00:50:10,441 --> 00:50:12,142
Nothing to say, right?

764
00:50:12,209 --> 00:50:14,645
So let's drop the false hope and quit.

765
00:50:14,712 --> 00:50:18,682
A dream is just a dream.

766
00:50:18,749 --> 00:50:22,319
No matter how hard we struggle,
some things just don't work out.

767
00:50:22,987 --> 00:50:24,455
I can't do this anymore.

768
00:50:24,522 --> 00:50:28,292
I'll take over the pig trotters shop.
That suits me better.

769
00:50:29,159 --> 00:50:31,629
That's all I was ever good for anyway.

770
00:50:34,632 --> 00:50:36,500
I'm sorry.

771
00:50:36,567 --> 00:50:38,135
I'll head out first.

772
00:50:38,202 --> 00:50:40,838
-Hey, Ki-jun!
-Don't stop him.

773
00:50:42,773 --> 00:50:46,343
-But still…
-We're too ashamed to ask him to stay.

774
00:50:46,410 --> 00:50:48,212
Nothing Ki-jun said was wrong.

775
00:50:52,182 --> 00:50:54,585
You guys can leave too if you want.

776
00:50:55,953 --> 00:50:57,888
I won't hold it against you.

777
00:51:00,724 --> 00:51:03,928
Buy some cabbage! Fresh cabbage here!

778
00:51:03,994 --> 00:51:05,663
Buy… Oh, need any cabbage?

779
00:51:05,729 --> 00:51:06,931
But it's so fresh.

780
00:51:06,997 --> 00:51:09,934
Buy some cabbage, ladies!
We have fresh cabbage!

781
00:51:10,000 --> 00:51:11,168
Ladies!

782
00:51:11,235 --> 00:51:13,837
-Buy some cabbage!

783
00:51:13,904 --> 00:51:17,107
-Buy some cabbage! It's so fresh!
-Come look at our cabbage!

784
00:51:21,946 --> 00:51:23,814
I wonder if they sold much cabbage.

785
00:51:24,481 --> 00:51:27,351
Cabbage? Right, those brats.

786
00:51:27,418 --> 00:51:30,254
You said they went
to sell cabbage in Seoul today.

787
00:51:31,121 --> 00:51:33,023
But why are you worried about that?

788
00:51:34,458 --> 00:51:36,660
Huh? No reason.

789
00:51:36,727 --> 00:51:39,129
They farmed so hard,
so I hope they do well.

790
00:51:39,196 --> 00:51:41,699
Why would you worry about that?

791
00:51:41,765 --> 00:51:44,535
On this cold winter night,
with no clue where it is,

792
00:51:44,602 --> 00:51:48,772
we have to hunt for five billion won.
We're way more pitiful, you dummy!

793
00:51:48,839 --> 00:51:50,608
Get up already.

794
00:51:50,674 --> 00:51:52,843
Fine, I'm going!

795
00:52:28,679 --> 00:52:30,981
Hey, let's just go play some pool.

796
00:52:31,048 --> 00:52:32,383
Nothing better to do?

797
00:52:32,449 --> 00:52:33,384
PARK MUN-SAM

798
00:52:33,450 --> 00:52:35,486
Do we have time to go play pool now?

799
00:52:35,552 --> 00:52:37,154
Use your head, jeez.

800
00:52:37,221 --> 00:52:40,491
What's the point of staring
at a guy who just sleeps all day?

801
00:52:40,557 --> 00:52:42,726
Just going for a game of pool

802
00:52:42,793 --> 00:52:44,828
and black bean noodles is way better.

803
00:52:44,895 --> 00:52:46,530
Black bean noodles?

804
00:52:49,199 --> 00:52:50,868
If you're going, go alone.

805
00:52:52,002 --> 00:52:54,471
What a jerk, jeez.

806
00:53:02,212 --> 00:53:03,847
-Where'd he go?
-Oh, crap.

807
00:53:08,152 --> 00:53:09,186
Nurse!

808
00:53:09,253 --> 00:53:11,121
Darn it!

809
00:53:12,222 --> 00:53:14,024
My goodness.

810
00:53:14,858 --> 00:53:16,326
Gosh.

811
00:53:16,393 --> 00:53:18,195
Hello? Hey, Hyeok.

812
00:53:18,262 --> 00:53:20,531
Why aren't you guys back yet?

813
00:53:21,899 --> 00:53:23,367
What?

814
00:53:23,434 --> 00:53:26,270
Oh, no. Okay, got it.

815
00:53:26,336 --> 00:53:28,672
Okay, take care of yourselves.

816
00:53:29,339 --> 00:53:30,874
Bye.

817
00:53:30,941 --> 00:53:32,576
Why? What did he say?

818
00:53:32,643 --> 00:53:34,178
He says they sold no cabbage

819
00:53:34,244 --> 00:53:36,113
and will stay in Seoul overnight.

820
00:53:36,180 --> 00:53:38,816
They must be trying to save on gas.

821
00:53:38,882 --> 00:53:40,818
I suppose so.

822
00:53:40,884 --> 00:53:42,086
Right.

823
00:53:42,152 --> 00:53:45,689
But where do those boys plan to sleep?

824
00:53:45,756 --> 00:53:48,225
That's what I'm saying.

825
00:54:01,405 --> 00:54:03,073
You all worked hard today.

826
00:54:03,140 --> 00:54:05,809
I'm sure they'll sell better tomorrow.

827
00:54:06,510 --> 00:54:08,212
Let's hurry and get some sleep.

828
00:54:08,278 --> 00:54:12,850
If I sleep like this,
my mouth might freeze up crooked.

829
00:54:13,817 --> 00:54:15,385
I'm going to sleep.

830
00:54:29,933 --> 00:54:32,436
-Aren't you helping?
-Ow, hey, stop that.

831
00:54:32,503 --> 00:54:35,806
I must've slept wrong.
My neck hurts, and I can't turn it.

832
00:54:35,873 --> 00:54:38,075
My whole body's aching like crazy too.

833
00:54:38,142 --> 00:54:40,210
Stop yapping and unload them quickly.

834
00:54:40,277 --> 00:54:43,046
We have to sell it all today, got it?

835
00:54:43,113 --> 00:54:46,550
Okay, let's pour our souls into today!

836
00:54:46,617 --> 00:54:48,752
Right. Hey, in that case,

837
00:54:48,819 --> 00:54:50,687
what if we try a delivery service?

838
00:54:50,754 --> 00:54:53,056
It's tough, but won't they sell well?

839
00:54:53,123 --> 00:54:54,858
-Oh, that's a good idea.
-Right?

840
00:54:54,925 --> 00:54:58,162
-But you do the deliveries.
-Oh, forget I said anything.

841
00:54:58,228 --> 00:55:00,130
-Ow.
-Give it here, give it here.

842
00:55:00,731 --> 00:55:02,065
Set it down.

843
00:55:04,468 --> 00:55:05,869
-Hey, hey.
-Huh?

844
00:55:05,936 --> 00:55:07,504
What's that over there?

845
00:55:08,639 --> 00:55:09,740
What's going on?

846
00:55:09,807 --> 00:55:13,510
-They're here again!
-It's a crackdown!

847
00:55:15,145 --> 00:55:16,980
It's a crackdown! A crackdown!

848
00:55:17,681 --> 00:55:19,583
Sir, why are you doing that?

849
00:55:19,650 --> 00:55:21,618
What are you doing? It's a crackdown!

850
00:55:21,685 --> 00:55:23,053
Quick, pack your stuff!

851
00:55:23,887 --> 00:55:25,455
-What's this about?
-No idea.

852
00:55:25,522 --> 00:55:28,592
-We did nothing wrong.
-We don't have to move too, do we?

853
00:55:28,659 --> 00:55:30,794
What are you people doing here, huh?

854
00:55:30,861 --> 00:55:32,262
-Load the truck!
-Yes.

855
00:55:32,329 --> 00:55:34,298
Wait, mister, what are you doing?

856
00:55:34,364 --> 00:55:36,099
-Mister!

857
00:55:36,166 --> 00:55:38,535
This is ours! It's ours!

858
00:55:41,271 --> 00:55:42,739
I said it's ours!

859
00:55:50,747 --> 00:55:53,917
Oh, hello? Hey, Hyeok.

860
00:55:53,984 --> 00:55:55,752
You guys are almost here?

861
00:55:55,819 --> 00:55:58,322
My goodness, you sold it all already?

862
00:56:00,390 --> 00:56:02,559
What? A crackdown?

863
00:56:02,626 --> 00:56:04,094
Oh, dear. Okay, got it.

864
00:56:04,761 --> 00:56:08,298
Okay, be careful and hurry back.

865
00:56:09,199 --> 00:56:11,168
What do you mean? A crackdown?

866
00:56:12,002 --> 00:56:14,071
He says they got caught in a crackdown

867
00:56:14,137 --> 00:56:16,073
and even lost all the cabbages.

868
00:56:16,139 --> 00:56:17,174
What?

869
00:56:17,241 --> 00:56:19,610
Oh, dear, what are they going to do?

870
00:56:19,676 --> 00:56:21,345
Tell me about it.

871
00:56:21,411 --> 00:56:24,214
They're almost here. I should go out.

872
00:56:27,084 --> 00:56:29,653
Please stay here. I'll go.

873
00:56:29,720 --> 00:56:31,688
Oh, really? Then let's go together…

874
00:56:31,755 --> 00:56:34,424
No, I'll just go by myself.

875
00:56:53,343 --> 00:56:54,912
Yu-na.

876
00:56:55,746 --> 00:56:57,214
Why come out in the cold?

877
00:56:57,281 --> 00:56:58,715
I just came to meet you.

878
00:57:00,851 --> 00:57:03,620
I heard you got caught in a crackdown.
Are you okay?

879
00:57:03,687 --> 00:57:05,455
I'm okay.

880
00:57:07,891 --> 00:57:09,927
By the way, where's Ki-jun?

881
00:57:10,427 --> 00:57:13,830
He got fed up with me and went home.

882
00:57:16,033 --> 00:57:17,801
Oh, really?

883
00:57:19,970 --> 00:57:22,139
I'll head inside first.

884
00:57:27,044 --> 00:57:28,612
Um, listen…

885
00:57:28,679 --> 00:57:32,316
I'm sorry about a few days ago.
I think I was too harsh on you.

886
00:57:32,983 --> 00:57:35,719
No, it was my mistake anyway.

887
00:57:37,087 --> 00:57:39,756
How about a walk to clear our heads?

888
00:57:39,823 --> 00:57:41,358
But you must be tired.

889
00:57:41,425 --> 00:57:43,560
I'm just feeling a bit down.

890
00:57:44,194 --> 00:57:46,129
Won't you cheer me up?

891
00:57:46,830 --> 00:57:48,165
Okay, sure.

892
00:57:48,231 --> 00:57:49,900
Let's go.

893
00:57:54,838 --> 00:57:58,742
They said they were almost back.
Jeez, why aren't they here yet?

894
00:58:00,544 --> 00:58:03,380
And what's with Yu-na all of a sudden?

895
00:58:03,447 --> 00:58:05,082
That's so strange.

896
00:58:07,584 --> 00:58:08,986
Oh, you're back?

897
00:58:09,052 --> 00:58:12,289
Oh my goodness, are you guys okay?

898
00:58:14,157 --> 00:58:15,926
Wait, what happened to your face?

899
00:58:17,094 --> 00:58:18,929
Well, it just happened.

900
00:58:19,763 --> 00:58:21,865
What about Ki-jun and Min-gi?

901
00:58:24,101 --> 00:58:27,771
Ki-jun said he's staying in Seoul.
He must be exhausted.

902
00:58:27,838 --> 00:58:29,339
Really?

903
00:58:30,273 --> 00:58:33,510
He could've at least come to see me.
That jerk.

904
00:58:34,211 --> 00:58:35,946
What about Min-gi?

905
00:58:36,013 --> 00:58:37,948
I think he had to talk to Yu-na.

906
00:58:38,015 --> 00:58:40,283
Oh, I see.

907
00:58:40,350 --> 00:58:43,286
Go wash up. I'll fix you some food.

908
00:58:43,353 --> 00:58:45,422
You both worked so hard.

909
00:58:49,559 --> 00:58:50,894
Hey, let's go. Let's go.

910
00:59:01,238 --> 00:59:03,140
What brings you here?

911
00:59:03,206 --> 00:59:05,409
Aren't you busy with your concert?

912
00:59:05,475 --> 00:59:07,711
I have something to say to you.

913
00:59:08,378 --> 00:59:10,514
To me? What is it?

914
00:59:11,181 --> 00:59:14,384
I'm sorry. I was too flustered then.

915
00:59:15,052 --> 00:59:18,021
Forget it. I'm even more sorry.

916
00:59:18,789 --> 00:59:22,359
And about that person you saw then.

917
00:59:22,426 --> 00:59:24,694
Oh, that lady?

918
00:59:25,429 --> 00:59:29,499
Is she your girlfriend?
Are you two getting married?

919
00:59:30,767 --> 00:59:33,270
Yes, next spring.

920
00:59:34,704 --> 00:59:36,807
Oh, I see.

921
00:59:37,874 --> 00:59:40,143
That's wonderful. Congratulations.

922
00:59:40,210 --> 00:59:41,545
Um, Yun-hui.

923
00:59:42,112 --> 00:59:43,980
So, about that,

924
00:59:44,881 --> 00:59:47,350
could you keep this a secret?

925
00:59:47,417 --> 00:59:48,885
What?

926
00:59:48,952 --> 00:59:52,155
If this gets out,
it'll put me in a really tough spot.

927
00:59:52,856 --> 00:59:55,692
But I'll pay child support
until the child grows up.

928
00:59:56,426 --> 00:59:58,061
Child support?

929
00:59:58,995 --> 01:00:02,966
Just think of it as the best I can do
as the child's father.

930
01:00:03,667 --> 01:00:06,103
I don't need that, so don't bother.

931
01:00:06,169 --> 01:00:08,004
-But still--
-I won't tell anyone.

932
01:00:08,071 --> 01:00:09,606
I have no plans to blab

933
01:00:09,673 --> 01:00:11,741
or hurt you in the slightest,

934
01:00:11,808 --> 01:00:13,477
so don't worry.

935
01:00:19,249 --> 01:00:21,184
And it's Min-ho! Min-ho!

936
01:00:21,251 --> 01:00:23,253
-That's my son's name.
-Yun-hui.

937
01:00:23,320 --> 01:00:25,555
I told you I won't cause you trouble.

938
01:00:25,622 --> 01:00:27,390
So just leave, please.

939
01:00:29,326 --> 01:00:30,961
I'm sorry, Yun-hui.

940
01:00:32,028 --> 01:00:34,431
Still, give it some thought.

941
01:00:55,485 --> 01:00:57,354
Let's get going, Min-gi.

942
01:00:58,622 --> 01:01:00,257
Okay.

943
01:01:03,226 --> 01:01:04,761
Min-gi.

944
01:01:05,428 --> 01:01:07,030
What's wrong?

945
01:01:07,097 --> 01:01:10,133
You go on ahead.
I need to stop somewhere first.

946
01:01:10,200 --> 01:01:12,102
LEE HYEON-SEOK

947
01:01:12,169 --> 01:01:15,305
Hey, man, where have you been
right before the concert?

948
01:01:15,372 --> 01:01:18,108
Any later and you'd have been
a no-show! A no-show!

949
01:01:18,942 --> 01:01:20,143
I'm sorry.

950
01:01:20,210 --> 01:01:21,912
I had to stop by somewhere.

951
01:01:26,183 --> 01:01:28,852
Who are you? You can't come in here.

952
01:01:29,519 --> 01:01:31,788
-Please leave.
-Out of my way.

953
01:01:34,791 --> 01:01:36,092
Lee Hyeon-seok?

954
01:01:37,727 --> 01:01:39,963
And who are you?

955
01:01:42,799 --> 01:01:44,768
-Argh!
-Hyeon-seok!

956
01:01:44,834 --> 01:01:46,436
Are you okay?

957
01:01:47,671 --> 01:01:50,740
What are you doing? Who are you?

958
01:01:50,807 --> 01:01:53,777
Me? I'm Yun-hui's close friend

959
01:01:53,843 --> 01:01:55,879
and Min-ho's uncle, you bastard!
